# Which Supabase Cloud project the Nexus tools on the Windows PC work on
# (npm run cloud:status, cloud:migrate, cloud:account, test:security:cloud),
# and what the cloud desktop app is built with (npm run desktop:build:cloud
# uses only the project id and the publishable key). See docs/cloud-setup.md
# and docs/desktop-app.md.
#
# Copy this file to .env.cloud.local (never committed) and fill it in. None of
# these values is secret. NEVER put the database password or a secret key
# (sb_secret_...) in this file or any other: the tools ask for them each time,
# hidden, and never store them.
#
#   NEXUS_CLOUD_PROJECT_REF      Project Settings → General → Project ID (20 characters)
#   NEXUS_CLOUD_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  Project Settings → API Keys → the publishable key (sb_publishable_...)
#   NEXUS_CLOUD_DB_HOST          Connect → Session pooler → only the host part of the address,
#                                for example aws-0-eu-west-2.pooler.supabase.com
#
# Also needed, in the project folder: the certificate from Project Settings →
# Database → SSL Configuration → Download certificate, saved as supabase-ca.crt.

NEXUS_CLOUD_PROJECT_REF=
NEXUS_CLOUD_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXUS_CLOUD_DB_HOST=
